# Shell scripts must reach Linux with LF endings.
#
# Git on Windows converts to CRLF on checkout by default, and a CRLF entrypoint
# fails inside a container with "no such file or directory" — pointing at a file
# that is plainly there, because the kernel is looking for an interpreter named
# "/usr/bin/env bash\r". Nothing in the message says so.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.conf text eol=lf
